~ start
The sun didn't come out today, but at least the rain stopped. 

It's November 7. One day left!

NANAY: Ollie, anak! Are you done? We need to leave for the supermarket while the dirt paths are still dry!

VALERIE: Ollie, hurry up. We need to buy the candles, the rice and... well, we still need to find the ingredients for your cake tomorrow. Move fast!

Everyone is waiting by the front door. I better prepare myself before going out. 


#AFTER GOING TO THE FRONT DOOR

PILI: There you are. Tie your shoes quickly. The rain has stopped for now, so we need to head to the supermarket while the paths are clear and the stores are still open.

OLLIE: Where is Tatay and Kuya Dodong? Oh and Noni?

VALERIE: They already went out to the fields early this morning, Ollie. Tatay said they need to check the ropes on the tarpaulin roofs after last night's wind. They're staying behind to finish securing the copra beds.

PILI: I hope your Tatay and Kuya Dodong are doing alright back at the farm. And our Noni... I can't believe he refused to come with us just so he could help them. Tying down those heavy tarpaulins in that wind must be exhausting... We should buy a few extra snacks for them. They'll be starving when they finish.

VALERIE: You know how Noni is, Nay. He follows Dodong everywhere.
VALERIE: Don't worry, Nay. I'm sure they'll be fine. Come on, Ollie, carry the big eco-bag. We still need to find the ingredients for your birthday cake tomorrow!

KIKI: Cake! Go out! Go vroom-vroom in tricycle!

PILI: Alright, let's go before the sky changes its mind again. Hold your sister's hand, Valerie.

#TIMESKIP

=> END